From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 10:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 61/61] PC5: a folder made in a user's folders gets its missing
 parents (Wine patch 0940)

A game copied from a PC was never installed on the console, so the
folders its installer made in the user's own folders aren't there. Call
of Juarez Gunslinger's engine makes AppData\Local\Techland\COJGunslinger
and stopped with an uncaught C++ exception when Techland wasn't there.
Wine now makes the missing parents of a folder a program makes under
C:\users\<name>\, as the installer would have; nothing outside the
users' folders changes.
